WEBVTT

00:37.176 --> 00:41.418
We step to shore in a different age A thousand

00:41.518 --> 00:45.900
miles from the open stage The waves deep and the

00:46.020 --> 00:51.823
current strong We hum the tune of a faded song The

00:51.903 --> 00:56.525
radio plays a foreign sound But we are drifting

00:56.545 --> 00:59.507
above the ground

01:01.868 --> 01:09.237
Like strangers in the stream Waiting for the

01:09.297 --> 01:13.439
dawn to break the dream

01:16.480 --> 01:24.363
Holding on to what we used to know Another place,

01:25.384 --> 01:32.167
another time ago Strangers in the street

01:38.497 --> 01:43.439
The layers pile by the open door A shadow falls on

01:43.479 --> 01:48.541
the wooden floor I see your face in the pan glass

01:49.322 --> 01:53.424
And watch the days as they slowly pass We row

01:53.484 --> 01:57.565
against an invisible tide With nowhere left for

01:57.606 --> 02:00.127
the ghost to hide

02:02.928 --> 02:10.228
Like strangers in the street Waiting for the

02:10.288 --> 02:14.310
dawn to break the dream

02:17.412 --> 02:24.475
Holding on to what we used to know I'm a third

02:24.555 --> 02:31.799
place and a third time ago Strangers in the

02:31.819 --> 02:32.319
street

02:36.785 --> 02:42.287
Is I a mirror of time? A mountain we have to climb

02:42.507 --> 02:46.968
The where is cold, the where is wide We have to

02:46.988 --> 02:48.069
reach the

02:53.070 --> 02:54.451
other side

03:19.553 --> 03:26.754
Like strangers in the street Waiting for the

03:26.834 --> 03:30.755
dawn to break that dream

03:33.936 --> 03:41.597
Holding on to what we used to know Another place,

03:42.738 --> 03:49.207
another time ago Strangers in the stream

03:53.551 --> 03:59.195
Strangers in the stream Waiting for the dawn

